<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    PATH 1, direct mapping, on the DEFAULT entity manager.

    Two columns, and the primary key is the whole point: ADR 009 rule 9 makes the `jti` the row, so
    "is this token revoked" is a lookup by identity and never a filter. That is what keeps a check
    running on every authenticated request cheap enough to be a rule rather than an aspiration.

    The type is `Id`, registered once for the whole project in config/packages/doctrine.php, because
    a `jti` is an identifier like every other one in this tree (ADR 002) and is minted as a ULID by
    `AccessTokens::issue()`. That also means the column takes the same platform-dependent shape as
    every other identifier here, GUID or binary(16), rather than being a second opinion about how an
    identifier is stored.

    It shares the `UiSecurity` mapping directory with `Credential.orm.xml` because it shares its
    namespace prefix, and Doctrine's MappingDriverChain gives one prefix one directory. It does not
    share anything else: ADR 009's table splits the two precisely because they have different
    lifetimes, and the day somebody wants to know which credential a revoked token belonged to, the
    answer is that the question is not asked here (see `RevokedToken`'s docblock).

    No `member_id`, no `revoked_by`, no `reason`. Each of those is an audit trail growing in a table
    that is not one, and ADR 008 is explicit that an audit trail with retention, search and legal
    weight is a product rather than a column somebody adds. `bin/console app:tokens:revoke` writes
    the log line instead.

    `revoked_at` carries an index because the only query anybody will ever want over this table is
    the sweep ADR 009 describes, deleting rows older than `AccessTokens::LIFETIME`, whose `jti` can
    no longer verify anyway. Nothing sweeps yet and `RevokedToken`'s docblock says so.
-->
<doctrine-mapping xmlns="http://doctrine-project.org/schemas/orm/doctrine-mapping"
                  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                  xsi:schemaLocation="http://doctrine-project.org/schemas/orm/doctrine-mapping https://www.doctrine-project.org/schemas/orm/doctrine-mapping.xsd">
    <entity name="App\Shared\Infrastructure\Security\RevokedToken" table="ui_revoked_token">
        <indexes>
            <index name="idx_revoked_token_revoked_at" columns="revoked_at"/>
        </indexes>

        <id name="jti" type="Id" column="jti">
            <generator strategy="NONE"/>
        </id>

        <field name="revokedAt" type="datetime_immutable" column="revoked_at" nullable="false"/>
    </entity>
</doctrine-mapping>
